From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] apklayer: no deferred swapchain image memory over a host Vulkan driver

VK_SWAPCHAIN_CREATE_DEFERRED_MEMORY_ALLOCATION_BIT_EXT (ANGLE sets it) makes the loader call vkCreateImage with a
VkImageSwapchainCreateInfoKHR that names the loader's own Swapchain object. Over a host driver that reaches the host's
vkCreateImage, which dereferences the handle as its own WSI swapchain (Mesa: a NULL device inside, SIGSEGV on a
vkCreateImage dispatch trampoline). The flag is only permission to defer: allocating the buffers up front (the loader's
non-deferred path, native-buffer images the HAL imports) is valid.
Against frameworks/native 46018f54b424 (REVISION), after 0003.
---
--- a/vulkan/libvulkan/swapchain.cpp
+++ b/vulkan/libvulkan/swapchain.cpp
@@ -2342,5 +2342,6 @@
     // Note: don't do deferred allocation for shared present modes. There's only one buffer
     // involved so very little benefit.
-    if ((create_info->flags & VK_SWAPCHAIN_CREATE_DEFERRED_MEMORY_ALLOCATION_BIT_EXT) &&
+    // apklayer patch: the host driver cannot create images for the loader's swapchain handle.
+    if (!driver::HostDispatchEnabled() && (create_info->flags & VK_SWAPCHAIN_CREATE_DEFERRED_MEMORY_ALLOCATION_BIT_EXT) &&
             !IsSharedPresentMode(create_info->presentMode)) {
         // Don't want to touch the underlying gralloc buffers yet;
